# MDXL — quick tour

-# Plain text, expressive output
-## One document, several renderers
-### Explore the extra layer

#### Syntax that stays readable

A signal: /col//green light /col#B7F77A// and //hl//something to notice//hl//.

Try /rbw//rainbow text//rbw//, /red//deprecated wording/red//, or a shortcut such as //key//Ctrl+C//key//.

Progress: /bar//72//. Hidden note: ||||[you found the invisible ink]||||.

This text flips: /!!!/Hello MDXL 42/!!!/

Navigate [[==>>]] forward, [[<<==]] backward, or use [[<=>>]] when both directions matter.

:check: Standard Markdown still works: **bold**, *italic*, inline code, lists, links, and tables.

`````python
# Five backticks make a copyable MDXL code block.
print("Nothing runs automatically.")
```
